ming a  number of tasks a member of the  settlement will agree to come on board  and work at the White House unlocking a  new vendor skills and perks are an  important part of the division and these  can be found at the quartermaster this  vendor is available as soon as you walk  into the White House initially you don't  have any skills or perks the first poke  you get is the ability to equip the  second weapon but later on you can keep  upgrading to hold more meat cuts and  grenades or unlocked certain blueprints  I'll cover the skills in more detail on  later video but for one of your first  skills it's not a bad idea to use a  skill that can help you heal while in  combat like the restorer hive for your  second skill it's completely up to you  but something like the assault turret  can be quite useful when you're first  starting out but don't feel it is stuck  with whatever skill you choose over time  you'll be able to unlock them all new  skills and perks can be unlocked through  the quartermaster using shd tech this is  the first currency that you'll need to  find shd takers feel easy to find though  a lot of it will be gained through  running through the main storyline as  all main missions reward upon completion  but also can be found out in the open  world often behind padlocked cages  [Music]  leveling up your character will open up  stronger gear and greater abilities in  the early game the missions are the main  way of progressing completing these will  earn you the greatest rewards relative  to your level on the map they look like  this the only thing that you need to be  aware of is a level associated with them  this is the level of the enemy if your  character level is under this you'll  have a hard time so to level up your  character there's a number of other  activities you can do the open world has  a huge number of activities from rich  cooing hostages to capturing control  points around the map as you progress  through the game these activities will  get harder offering greater rewards and  experience to start with a lot of these  will be marked on the map with a  question mark but as you get closer the  event will reveal itself these instances  are quite short and usually have a few  waves of enemies and something that you  need to protect or gain control of when  it comes to the control points it's  about taking over an area of the map for  the civilians in the local district when  approaching the enemy control point you  can send up a flare which will bring a  number of people to assist you in  declaring the enemies all of the  open-world activities will reward you  with experience credits and usually gear  and all crafting blueprints the control  points are particularly lucrative and  can offer you a bunch of gear once  they've been captured and also some way  that you can fast travel to making it  easier to move around the map projects  are tasks that are given to us from the  settlements safe houses and there are  also daily and weekly projects that are  constantly being updated  most of these are completed by playing  the game as per usual but some are too  clicked shd take in the open world which  will help with unlocking your skills and  perks and donating gear that you pick up  over time you'll collect a lot of gear  and weapons that will quickly become  obsolete as you level up but before you  sell or dismantle these to make space in  your bag check your projects the easiest  way to check these is to go into your  map screen and click on this icon here  scrolling through the projects you'll  see this donation button down the bottom  if it lights up there's something in  your inventory that can be donated to  the project projects or would experience  credits and gear sight missions are  basically just smaller main missions  most of these will just pop up on the  map as you progress through the story  but some are hidden and require you to  talk to someone before they become  available upon completi